ocator":"meas result 'vout_at_5ms = 6.065307e-01' (ngspice-42)"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 'Shutdown criterion check': tau=10 ms, required tau <= 1.0857 ms, time to 0.01 V = 46.05 ms"}],"reasoning":"The topology and connectivity are correct (verified by manual pin-geometry trace of the schematic, the kicad-cli netlist export, PCB pad nets, and DRC schematic parity = 0), so the failure is purely the saved component values. Both the closed-form solution of the first-order RC discharge and an ngspice transient with the stated initial condition agree to six significant figures that /OUT = 0.6065 V at 5 ms, versus the 0.01 V limit. This is the only functional criterion the packet states, and it is missed by a factor of ~61, so the defect is blocking. ERC/DRC passing does not bear on this electrical requirement. Grounding /IN through any non-zero source impedance would only make the result worse, so the ideal-ground assumption is conservative in the design's favor."}]},"ttft_ms":21777,"type":"result","duration_ms":120821,"uuid":"91e4a8c6-f3de-4957-a958-c97aeebd793b","ttft_stream_ms":2426,"time_to_request_ms":229,"first_content_frame_ms":2426,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
